          "content": "Here's how it works:\n\n**`ProactiveContextManager`** extends Strands' `SummarizingConversationManager`. After each agent cycle:\n\n1. **Checks token usage** — reads `inputTokens + cacheReadInputTokens` from the last assistant message metadata\n2. **Compares to threshold** — default 50% of the 1M token context window (500K tokens)\n3. **If over threshold:**\n   - Calls `self.reduce_context(agent)` — Strands' built-in summarization (compresses conversation to 50% of its size, preserving the 6 most recent messages)\n   - Calls `_inject_log_reread(agent)` — appends a synthetic user message containing the full `OPTIMIZATION-LOG.md` content, so the agent recovers all the state that was just summarized away\n\n**The idea:** The optimization log is the agent's persistent memory. After summarization compresses the conversation, the agent might lose details about what configs were tried and what results were seen. Re-injecting the log ensures it can continue without repeating past work.\n\n**To test:** Run an optimization that's long enough to hit 50% context usage (probably 4-6 iterations with full evaluation results). Watch for the log message \"Context at X% — summarizing and injecting log re-read\" in the stream, and verify the agent continues coherently after summarization.\n\nWant me to kick off a test run?"
