          "content": "\n\nThat's how it works now. Here's why:\n\n- **Cost:** `CostTrackingHook` accumulates cost in DynamoDB based on `accumulated_usage` from Strands (total tokens used across the entire session). Summarization doesn't reset this — it's a running total. Cost only goes up.\n\n- **Context %:** The `ProactiveContextManager` calculates percentage from `inputTokens + cacheReadInputTokens` in the *last assistant message's metadata*. After summarization compresses the conversation (removes old messages, replaces with a summary), the next model call sends fewer input tokens → the percentage drops.\n\nSo yes — cost keeps climbing, context % drops after summarization. No additional code needed."
